      "page_title": "systemd 101: PID 1, Units & systemctl",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "PID 1",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "systemd is PID 1 — the init system that starts, supervises and stops every user-space process."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "starts everything in parallel at boot",
            "cgroups track each spawned process",
            "stays supervisor for the whole runtime"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Unit Types"
        },
        {
